{
  "actual_observations": null,
  "assumptions": [
    "Keep the selected current geometry, hardware, six original fields, 100 bolts and 66 Hillman axes. Use only cached BREP queries, exact action recovery and static section LPs. No new frame/native FEA response, CAD model rebuild or redesign.",
    "Reuse the authenticated local-timber-v2 source report and all of its source bindings. Recover its original signed point actions, their own host datums and free couples, and the same affine selfweight mass/centroid. Preserve tiny nonzero forces and couples.",
    "The assessed interval is the minimum-to-maximum station of the six earlier top-rail queries. Enumerate every nonzero point-action event inside it separately in each case; no station grouping or point-load shift. Source endpoints at each event are evaluated before and after their actual actions.",
    "The grain is exactly X. Use an exactly orthonormal rational frame parameterized by the recorded half-tangent. Transform the source binary positions/forces/couples exactly. Only nominal projected CAD vertices round to eight decimals, with their exact rounding error recorded.",
    "The projected convex-quadrilateral vertex envelope of 2e-6 mm is an explicit numerical geometry assumption, including CAD/projection/rounding uncertainty; it is not a certified universal CAD error theorem or a physical cut tolerance. A 1e-4-mm inset and exact expanded-corner containment construct robust inner rectangles.",
    "Capture each cached BREP once, verify its byte buffer and import that in-memory snapshot. Cached-solid Boolean queries must show each of three continuous inner prisms has zero material outside the finished rail, and that the finished rail has zero material outside its original planar/straight-edged raw stock. Raw-stock projected vertex extrema plus the envelope give a conservative outer section rectangle. No cached BREP bytes change or duplicate.",
    "For a plane normal to grain, use the additional unobserved C16 reference envelope: tension parallel 8.5 MPa, compression parallel 17 MPa, and both longitudinal shear components 3.2*0.67=2.144 MPa. Table 3.3 printed p.10 supplies C16 strengths; p.25 supplies the conservative crack-width factor. The helper key rolling_shear is only its legacy second-shear slot; this plane uses longitudinal shear in both directions, not the cleat rolling-shear approximation.",
    "The pointwise section hypothesis is max(sigma/Ft,-sigma/Fc)+abs(tau_p)/Fv+abs(tau_q)/Fv<=u. Retain the existing six divisor/action scenarios, including working divisor 2. This is an engineering comparison, not a generic NDS DF-L No.2 grade/capacity assignment or an authenticated EC5 ULS check.",
    "Bilinear corner tractions are selected by an LP. Exact polynomial integration plus a six-resultant correction recovers all N,Vp,Vq,T,Mp,Mq. Existing Bernstein bounds certify the continuous pointwise interaction. A selected LP objective or dual is not optimality, feasibility or resistance proof.",
    "Between source point events, the unchanged affine gravity and fixed preceding point actions give a complete cut wrench of degree at most three in station. Four exact cubic Bernstein control fields on the common corridors yield, by convexity, a sufficient section-field upper bound at every station. These controls are generally synthetic wrenches, not newly predicted physical demands.",
    "Necessary lower bounds are evaluated only on actual source-polynomial stations using exact continuous support integrals over an outer rectangle. A failed synthetic control upper is inconclusive; only an actual-station necessary lower above one proves this declared section hypothesis fails.",
    "Continuous section traction feasibility and modeled material corridors do not establish per-piece three-dimensional stress equilibrium, inter-piece or bore load transfer, free side tractions, elastic compatibility, buckling, fracture, complete joint/member resistance or physical stiffness/demand bounds. Keep those full qualifications explicit.",
    "Preserve deferred panel/screw exceedances, excluded actual fit, blank observations, rejected-proposal history, foreign files/index and all frozen source/results. No staging, publication, archive or pruning."
  ],
